      <description>&lt;div class="wi_fic_desc" property="description"&gt;&lt;p&gt;Hounds are useful tools, certainly. Devastating weapons turned against their former comrades. But what happens when, inevitably, even the finest sword breaks?&lt;/p&gt; &lt;p&gt;Abandoned by her Handler and cast to the side by the empire that broke her, rebel hero-turned-Hound-turned-stray Alida Chondax finds herself far away from the war that once ruled her life. In a quiet, rural region of her homeworld, where neither rebel nor Imperial bothers to go, she is taken in by the kindness of strangers, and a once-loyal Hound is left to finally heal. But can a dog of war so broken ever truly recover?&lt;/p&gt; &lt;p&gt;Meanwhile, her old friend, Jaxie Thornth, finds herself in the place Alida once held, the new prize possession of her Handler. But war is a cruel mistress, and Death looms fickly around every corner. Nobody - neither stern veteran nor most ironclad officer - is immune to its vagaries.&lt;/p&gt; &lt;p&gt;What happens to a Hound when its master dies?&lt;/p&gt; &lt;/div&gt;</description>
