    <item>
      <title>The Soulflame Chronicles</title>
      <author> SylvieLAshwood </author>
      <link>https://www.scribblehub.com/series/2527153/the-soulflame-chronicles/</link>
      <comments>https://www.scribblehub.com/read/2527153-the-soulflame-chronicles/chapter/2527201/#comments</comments>
      <guid isPermaLink="false">919c31030175bcb4f658b886e4a7b180b57c0a2b</guid>
      <pubDate>Fri, 18 Sep 2026 22:17:27 +0000</pubDate>
      <description>&lt;div class="wi_fic_desc" property="description"&gt;&lt;p&gt;Luke Thompson expected another night playing Radiance Ember Soulflame, the ridiculously beautiful Crown Princess he had spent months building for an anonymous tabletop campaign. Instead, the game became real, and Radiance’s body became his body.&lt;/p&gt; &lt;p&gt;Her kingdom recognizes him. Her skills work even when he has no idea how he learned them, her instincts feel disturbingly natural, and the System insists that Radiance Ember Soulflame is exactly who he is supposed to be. At least the character sheet is familiar, or close enough to familiar to be useful.&lt;/p&gt; &lt;p&gt;Classes gain levels. Skills improve through use. Achievements unlock rewards. Backgrounds evolve through accomplishments. Her strange Soulflame Heritage has progression requirements the System refuses to explain. Apparently even being Crown Princess comes with mechanical advantages, provided Radiance can survive the responsibilities that come with the title.&lt;/p&gt; &lt;p&gt;There is no logout button, no guaranteed resurrection, and no walkthrough for becoming the woman whose life you are suddenly living. There is, however, Prince Adrian of Valenne: six-foot-six, absurdly handsome, heavily armed, relentlessly flirtatious, and apparently Radiance’s arranged fiancé, which Luke is fairly certain was never part of the character sheet.&lt;/p&gt; &lt;p&gt;The Soulflame Chronicles is a character-driven LitRPG fantasy featuring meaningful progression, evolving Classes and Heritages, quests and achievements, adventuring, royal politics, romance, and one very confused princess trying to figure out where the Player ends and Radiance begins.&lt;/p&gt; &lt;/div&gt;</description>
